        # result = {'jd_text': 'Summary\nWe are looking for Full-Stack AI / Agentic Engineers across junior and senior levels who blend enterprise software engineering with cutting-edge artificial intelligence. In this role, your expertise will be to design, build, and deploy robust applications using the .NET stack and Azure Infrastructure, while seamlessly integrating AI models and autonomous agentic frameworks.\nYou will participate in the end-to-end SDLC—ensuring applications follow clean code principles, architectural design patterns, and rigorous testing—to deliver scalable, production-ready enterprise AI solutions.\n \nResponsibilities:\nDesign and develop scalable, secure backend APIs and full-stack AI applications using C# and .NET Core.\nDevelop and integrate AI modules using frameworks such as Microsoft AutoGen, Semantic Kernel, and Azure OpenAI.\nApply robust software engineering design principles (SOLID, Clean Architecture, Design Patterns) to ensure maintainable codebases.\nImplement data engineering and preprocessing pipelines (OCR text extraction, data manipulation) to prepare data for model context or fine-tuning.\nArchitect and provision Azure cloud infrastructure (PaaS, Serverless, and Containerized solutions) ensuring proper networking, security, and identity management.\nDesign and implement fallback mechanics, guardrails, and validation layers to prevent agentic loops and AI drift.\nCollaborate with Solution Architects to deploy, monitor, and optimize machine learning algorithms and RAG architectures.\n \nRequired Skills & Qualifications\nCore Backend: Strong proficiency in C#, .NET Core, ASP.NET Web API, and Entity Framework.\nAzure Platform: Hands-on experience with Azure PaaS services (Azure App Services, Azure Function Apps, Azure Key Vault, Azure Entra ID / Managed Identities).\nAI Frameworks: Hands-on experience with Microsoft Agentic Framework / AutoGen, Azure AI Foundry, and Azure OpenAI service tools.\nData & AI Scripting: Proficiency 